================================================================================
astro4j / JSol'Ex
================================================================================

Portions of SolScan's spectral-line identification, exposure calculation, and SHG reconstruction
logic are translated and adapted from the astro4j project (JSol'Ex, JSol'Ex CLI, jsolex-core),
by Cedric Champeau ("melix") and contributors.
    https://github.com/melix/astro4j

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of the License is available at:
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

astro4j does not ship a NOTICE file of its own to propagate. Per-file attribution is instead
retained in the header of each SolScan source file that closely translates a specific astro4j
source file, pointing back to the original.

Specifically adapted, at time of writing (see CLAUDE.md for the full, current list; not yet
implemented, still on the roadmap):
  - DeepLineIdentifier (spectral line identification via reference-atlas correlation)
  - SpectralLineCatalog (interesting-lines.txt secondary-line lookup)
  - SpectrumBrowser (dispersion-aware reference-spectrum rendering)
  - ExposureCalculator (recommended exposure/fps from instrument optics and solar ephemeris)
  - SpectroHeliograph / Setup (equipment-profile data shapes)
  - SolexVideoProcessor's remaining pipeline (banding/jagging/distortion corrections, Advanced
    Images/Debug image kinds, ImageMath scripts) - its processSingleFrame reconstruction loop and
    geometry-correction stage (ellipse fitting, the shear/scale warp, autocrop) have landed, see below

Specifically adapted, actually landed (each also carries its own per-file header comment pointing
back to the original Java source, per CLAUDE.md):
  - SpectralRay (predefined spectral line catalog - SolScan.Core.Processing.SpectralRay)
  - LineDetectionMode, RotationKind, AutocropMode, ContrastEnhancement, GeneratedImageKind (process
    parameter enums - SolScan.Core.Processing)
  - SpectrumParams, GeometryParams, RequestedImages, ProcessParams (process parameter records,
    trimmed to the fields SolScan currently uses - see each type's own doc comment for what's
    deliberately excluded - SolScan.Core.Processing)
  - AverageImageCreator.computeAverageImage (SolScan.Processing.Shg.FrameAverager - ported as a
    sequential two-pass version, see its own doc comment)
  - SpectrumFrameAnalyzer's curve-fitting pipeline - findLocalMinimum/findMinima/
    findDistortionPolynomial/findPolynomialAround/refineFit/depthWeightedCenter/sigmaClippedFit
    (SolScan.Processing.Shg.SpectralLineCurvatureDetector - disk left/right border detection not
    ported, see its own doc comment for why that's a real, supported fallback mode of the original
    algorithm, not an invented shortcut)
  - LinearRegression.secondOrderRegression, both overloads (math module -
    SolScan.Processing.Math.LinearRegression)
  - SolexVideoProcessor.processSingleFrame - the 5-tap Gaussian-weighted reconstruction loop
    (SolScan.Processing.Shg.DiskReconstructor)
  - DirectoryKind, and GeneratedImageKind's own per-constant directoryKind() mapping (which output
    subfolder each generated image kind belongs in - SolScan.Core.Processing.DirectoryKind /
    GeneratedImageKindExtensions.GetDirectoryKind, folder-naming convention confirmed against
    NamingStrategyAwareImageEmitter.java)
  - Ellipse, EllipseRegression (math module - SolScan.Processing.Math.Ellipse/EllipseRegression;
    EllipseRegression's Halir-Flusser eigensystem solve is re-derived via a closed-form 3x3 cubic
    solver in the new SolScan.Processing.Math.Matrix3x3 rather than porting astro4j's own
    Apache-Commons-Math-backed DoubleMatrix, since SolScan.Processing has no such dependency - see
    Matrix3x3's own doc comment)
  - EllipseFittingTask's sample-finding/outlier-filtering/fit-retry pipeline (SolScan.Processing.Shg.
    DiskEdgeDetector) - one confirmed-dead step skipped, see DiskEdgeDetector's own header comment
  - BackgroundRemoval.blindBackgroundNeutralization/removeZeroPixels, and AnalysisUtils.
    estimateBlackPoint/estimateBackgroundLevel and util.Histogram (SolScan.Processing.Shg.
    BackgroundNeutralizer/ImageStatistics) - the 6-term background-model fit is solved via the new
    SolScan.Processing.Math.LinearSystem's plain Gaussian elimination in place of Apache Commons
    Math's OLSMultipleLinearRegression
  - GeometryTransform (SolScan.Processing.Math.GeometryTransform)
  - GeometryUtils.applyGeometryCorrection/computeCorrectedCircle (SolScan.Processing.Shg.
    GeometryResampler)
  - GeometryCorrector's autocrop step, and Cropper.cropToSquare/cropToRectangle
    (SolScan.Processing.Shg.DiskGeometryCorrector/DiskCropper)
  - SolexVideoProcessor's maybePerformFlips/maybePerformRotation (SolScan.Processing.Shg.
    DiskGeometryCorrector's mirror/rotation pre-step) - ported without the rotateLeft step that
    precedes them in the original, since SolScan's own DiskReconstructor output doesn't need it (see
    DiskGeometryCorrector's own header comment)
  - AutohistogramStrategy - the "AutoStretch" contrast-enhancement mode: iterative ellipse-aware
    background neutralization, CLAHE-blended prominence handling, gamma, asinh brightness matching, and
    an ellipse-faded contrast S-curve (SolScan.Processing.Stretching.AutoStretchStrategy) - two
    deliberate simplifications (adjustBrightness always true; protusStretch defaults to 0, still ported
    but short-circuited at that value since the curve is then provably the identity) - see
    AutoStretchStrategy's own header comment
  - ClaheStrategy, GammaStrategy, RangeExpansionStrategy, and the subset of Histogram AutoStretchStrategy
    uses (SolScan.Processing.Stretching) - ClaheStrategy/GammaStrategy's original OpenCL/GPU paths are
    dropped, SolScan.Processing having no such dependency
  - BackgroundRemoval.backgroundModel's degree-2 case, combined with AutohistogramStrategy's own
    neutralizeBg wrapper (SolScan.Processing.Shg.BackgroundNeutralizer.NeutralizeMasked) - solved via
    the existing SolScan.Processing.Math.LinearSystem plus a ridge-regularization term matching the
    original's own PENALTY constant, in place of Apache Commons Math
  - Ellipse's translate/rescale/boundingBox (SolScan.Processing.Math.Ellipse) - added alongside the
    members already ported for ellipse fitting/geometry correction
  - Clahe.applyMultiScaleClahe/computeTileSizesForImage/computeTileSizes/multiScaleClaheChannel
    ("CLAHE2" contrast enhancement - SolScan.Processing.Stretching.MultiScaleClaheStrategy) - the
    original's RGBImage per-channel branch dropped, SolScan.Processing having no colour image type
  - GeneratedImageKind.COLORIZED and its production pipeline - the first Advanced Images kind ported
    (SolScan.Core.Processing.GeneratedImageKind.Colorized/SolScan.Processing.Shg.ShgProcessor.ProduceColorizedImage):
    ProcessingWorkflow.produceColorizedImage's arcsinh-stretch-then-percentile-clip-then-colorize
    sequence (SolScan.Processing.Stretching.ArcsinhStretchingStrategy/PercentileStretchStrategy, CPU
    path only, GPU dropped as elsewhere), AnalysisUtils.estimateBlackPoint (already ported as
    SolScan.Processing.Shg.ImageStatistics.EstimateBlackPoint for geometry correction's own warp/crop
    fill colour - now also surfaced via DiskGeometryCorrector.Result.BlackPoint for this), ColorCurve/
    KnownCurves.H_ALPHA (SolScan.Core.Processing.ColorCurveParams data +
    SolScan.Processing.Color.ColorCurve math - the per-channel quadratic fit reuses the existing
    SolScan.Processing.Math.LinearRegression.SecondOrderRegression rather than porting the original's
    own hand-derived polynomial solve/cache; KnownCurves' own unused CALCIUM/HELIUM curves aren't
    ported, confirmed dead code even in the original), SpectralRay.toRGB/toSimpleRGB/improveEsthetics
    (SolScan.Core.Processing.SpectralRay.ToRgb, kept in Core as dependency-free math alongside that
    record's other data, same precedent as SolScan.Core.Astronomy.SunPosition), the
    Colorize.doColorize(width,height,mono,int[] rgb) wavelength-tint overload
    (SolScan.Processing.Color.Colorize.WithWavelengthRgb, reusing the already-ported GammaStrategy),
    and ImageUtils.fromRGBtoHSL/fromHSLtoRGB plus the generic StretchingStrategy.stretch(RGBImage)
    default method's one concrete use in this pipeline (SolScan.Processing.Color.RgbHsl/
    Colorize.StretchByLightness - ported as a direct specialization for the one stretch strategy
    (a plain min/max linear stretch, itself newly ported as SolScan.Processing.Stretching.LinearStretchStrategy)
    this pipeline actually drives through it, not a general RGBImage-stretch dispatch mechanism)

